22:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose prose-slate max-w-none dark:prose-invert prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:tracking-tight prose-p:leading-8 prose-a:text-blue-700","children":[["$","section","How to compare JSON formatters fairly",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"How to compare JSON formatters fairly"}],[["$","p","A JSON formatter should be judged on validation accuracy, readability, privacy, speed, output control, and how well it connects to the next debugging step. Pretty indentation is the baseline, not the differentiator.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"A JSON formatter should be judged on validation accuracy, readability, privacy, speed, output control, and how well it connects to the next debugging step. Pretty indentation is the baseline, not the differentiator."}]]}],["$","p","For sensitive payloads, local-first behavior matters. For large files, performance and folding matter. For API teams, diffing, schema generation, and format conversion often matter more than visual polish.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"For sensitive payloads, local-first behavior matters. For large files, performance and folding matter. For API teams, diffing, schema generation, and format conversion often matter more than visual polish."}]]}]]]}],["$","section","When ToolOrbit is a good fit",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"When ToolOrbit is a good fit"}],[["$","p","ToolOrbit works well when you need a quick browser-based formatter and may also need related utilities such as JSON to TypeScript, XML to JSON, text diff, URL encoding, or Base64 decoding. That makes it useful for debugging API payloads outside a full IDE or API client.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"ToolOrbit works well when you need a quick browser-based formatter and may also need related utilities such as JSON to TypeScript, XML to JSON, text diff, URL encoding, or Base64 decoding. That makes it useful for debugging API payloads outside a full IDE or API client."}]]}],["$","p","It is also useful for documentation and support workflows because links are easy to share and the interface is focused on the task rather than a full request management environment.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"It is also useful for documentation and support workflows because links are easy to share and the interface is focused on the task rather than a full request management environment."}]]}]]]}],["$","section","When another JSON formatter is better",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"When another JSON formatter is better"}],[["$","p","Use VS Code when the JSON is already part of a repository and you want project formatting rules. Use jq when you need repeatable filtering, extraction, or automation. Use Postman or Insomnia when the JSON response needs to be interpreted beside request headers, auth state, and environment variables.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Use VS Code when the JSON is already part of a repository and you want project formatting rules. Use jq when you need repeatable filtering, extraction, or automation. Use Postman or Insomnia when the JSON response needs to be interpreted beside request headers, auth state, and environment variables."}]]}],["$","p","The right answer is often a combination: use the API client to make the request, a browser formatter for quick sharing or inspection, and a diff tool to compare response versions.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"The right answer is often a combination: use the API client to make the request, a browser formatter for quick sharing or inspection, and a diff tool to compare response versions."}]]}]]]}],"$L29"]}]
